{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>פרוצה</b> — that has become a breach in its walls." "<b>אין חומה</b> — that no wall was built at the place of the breach, for people to pass through, and whoever wishes may go out. So too a man who has no restraint on his spirit — on his soul, to hold back his words. And behold, silence is good for them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:46.072004576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}